the east?\""}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1066, "end": 1143, "text": "Captain Orlova, a seasoned veteran of the Russian Navy, smiled enigmatically."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1144, "end": 1232, "text": "\"Let us just say, Lieutenant, that the winds of change are blowing across the continent."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1233, "end": 1377, "text": "The Soviet Union, as you know, is still in its infancy, but its leaders are already making bold moves to secure their place on the world stage.\""}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1378, "end": 1410, "text": "Mellersh's curiosity was piqued."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1411, "end": 1454, "text": "\"Go on,\" he urged, his eyes locked on hers."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1455, "end": 1506, "text": "Orlova leaned in, her voice barely above a whisper."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1507, "end": 1640, "text": "\"I have it on good authority that the Soviet high command is seeking to forge alliances with key military leaders from across Europe."}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1641, "end": 1731, "text": "And I believe you, Lieutenant Mellersh, have a crucial role to play in this grand design.\""}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1732, "end": 1900, "text": "As Mellersh listened, entranced, Orlova outlined a plan that would take him from the familiar waters of the Royal Navy to the uncharted territories of the Soviet Union."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1901, "end": 2040, "text": "It was a journey that would test his mettle, challenge his loyalties, and ultimately, propel him to the highest echelons of military power."}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2041, "end": 2173, "text": "The fire crackled, and the patrons of the tavern laughed and chatted, oblivious to the subtle machinations unfolding in their midst."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 19, "text": "**Arthur Mellersh**"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 21, "end": 110, "text": "Arthur Mellersh was a British Royal Navy officer who held the rank of lieutenant in 1837."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 111, "end": 136, "text": "**Early Life and Career**"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 138, "end": 209, "text": "There is limited information available on Arthur Mellersh's early life."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 210, "end": 311, "text": "However, it is known that he joined the Royal Navy and rose through the ranks to become a lieutenant."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 312, "end": 334, "text": "**Rank of Lieutenant**"}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 336, "end": 466, "text": "A lieutenant is a junior commissioned officer rank in the Royal Navy, ranking above sub-lieutenant and below lieutenant commander."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 467, "end": 565, "text": "The rank of lieutenant is equivalent to the rank of captain in the British Army and Royal Marines."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 566, "end": 586, "text": "**Evidence of Rank**"}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 588, "end": 684, "text": "According to the Navy List of 1837, Arthur Mellersh is listed as a lieutenant in the Royal Navy."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 685, "end": 870, "text": "[1] This publication, which was published quarterly by the British Admiralty, provided a comprehensive list of all officers in the Royal Navy, including their rank and ship assignments."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 871, "end": 998, "text": "Additionally, Mellersh's service record, held at the National Archives in Kew, London, confirms his rank as lieutenant in 1837."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 999, "end": 1002, "text": "[2]"}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1004, "end": 1018, "text": "**References**"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1020, "end": 1044, "text": "[1] The Navy List, 1837."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1045, "end": 1065, "text": "London: John Murray."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1066, "end": 1101, "text": "[2] National Archives, Kew, London."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1102, "end": 1136, "text": "ADM 196\\/1\\/144, Mellersh, Arthur."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1137, "end": 1152, "text": "Service Record."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Arthur Mellersh", "scope": "military rank", "claim": "Arthur Mellersh's military rank is Lieutenant.", "answer": "Lieutenant", "quote": "As the sun dipped into the horizon, casting a warm orange glow over the bustling streets of London, Lieutenant Arthur Mellersh made his way through the crowded tavern.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["Lieutenant"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Lieutenant", "origin": "initial"}]}
